---
description: How to find, read and write docs under docs/ with few tokens
globs: docs/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- Schema and full rules: `docs/README.md` (DOC-001). Every doc except
  `INDEX.md` has the frontmatter defined there.
- Retrieve in this order and stop as soon as you have enough:
  1. `docs/INDEX.md`, 2. the section `INDEX.md`, 3. only the docs you need.
     Follow `related` and `depends` one hop at a time.
- Direction (vision, architecture, decisions, roadmap): the `direction`
  table at the top of `docs/INDEX.md`, DES-014 to DES-017. Read it before
  structural changes; add a DES-016 row when a decision lands.
- Known id or tag: `rg -l '^id: DES-003' docs`, `rg -l '^tags: .*\bengine\b' docs`.
  To triage, read only the first 12 lines (frontmatter).
- Never read whole folders. Never edit `INDEX.md` by hand.
- Writing: one topic per doc, under 300 lines, lowercase-id file name
  (`des-009-run-view.md`), next free id, set `updated` to today.
- Backlog items need `## Done when`. Move `status` as work moves.
- After edits run `pnpm docs:index` then `pnpm docs:check` (the Cursor
  hook runs `docs:index` for you after agent edits).
